{{Short description|Parliamentary constituency in the United Kingdom, 2024 onwards}} {{Infobox UK constituency main |name = Harpenden and Berkhamsted |parliament = uk |image = {{maplink|frame=yes|frame-align=center|plain=yes|raw={{Wikipedia:Map data/Harpenden and Berkhamsted (UK Parliament constituency)}}|frame-height=200|frame-width=250}} |caption = Boundaries since 2024 |image2 = [[File:East of England - Harpenden and Berkhamsted constituency.svg|215px|alt=Map of constituency]] |caption2 = Boundary of Harpenden and Berkhamsted in the East of England |year = 2024 |abolished = |type = County |previous = [[Hitchin and Harpenden (UK Parliament constituency)|Hitchin and Harpenden]] & [[South West Hertfordshire (UK Parliament constituency)|South West Hertfordshire]] |next = |electorate = 71,635 (2023)<ref>{{cite web |url= https://boundarycommissionforengland.independent.gov.uk/2023-review/the-2023-review-of-parliamentary-constituency-boundaries-in-england-volume-two-constituency-names-designations-and-composition/the-2023-review-of-parliamentary-constituency-boundaries-in-england-volume-two-constituency-names-designations-and-composition-eastern/#lg_harpenden-and-berkhamsted-cc-71635 |title= The 2023 Review of Parliamentary Constituency Boundaries in England – Volume two: Constituency names, designations and composition – Eastern |publisher=Boundary Commission for England |access-date=26 June 2024 |df=dmy }}</ref> |mp = [[Victoria Collins]] |party = [[Liberal Democrats (UK)|Liberal Democrats]] |region = England |county = [[Hertfordshire]] |elects_howmany = One |towns = [[Harpenden]] and [[Berkhamsted]] }}
'''Harpenden and Berkhamsted''' is a [[List of UK Parliament constituencies|constituency]] of the [[House of Commons of the United Kingdom|House of Commons]] in the [[Parliament of the United Kingdom|UK Parliament]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=2023-06-30 |title=Hitchin and Harpenden set for shake-up after boundary review |url=https://www.thecomet.net/news/23625029.herts-major-changes-constituency-boundary-review/ |access-date=2024-02-10 |website=The Comet |language=en}}</ref> Further to the completion of the [[2023 Periodic Review of Westminster constituencies]], it was first contested at the [[2024 United Kingdom general election|2024 general election]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=The 2023 Review of Parliamentary Constituency Boundaries in England – Volume one: Report – Eastern {{!}} Boundary Commission for England |url=https://boundarycommissionforengland.independent.gov.uk/2023-review/2023-review-volume-one-report/the-2023-review-of-parliamentary-constituency-boundaries-in-england-volume-one-report-eastern/ |access-date=2023-07-14 |website=boundarycommissionforengland.independent.gov.uk}}</ref> The current MP is [[Victoria Collins]].
== Boundaries == The constituency is composed of the following (as they existed on 1 December 2020):
* The Borough of Dacorum wards of: Aldbury and Wigginton; Ashridge; Berkhamsted Castle; Berkhamsted East; Berkhamsted West; Northchurch; Tring Central; Tring East; Tring West and Rural; Watling.
* The City of St. Albans wards of: Harpenden East; Harpenden North; Harpenden South; Harpenden West; Redbourn; Sandridge; Wheathampstead.<ref name=":0">{{Cite web |title=The Parliamentary Constituencies Order 2023 |url=https://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/2023/1230/schedules/made |at=Schedule I Part 2 Eastern region}}</ref>
It comprises the following areas:
* [[Harpenden]], [[Redbourn]], [[Sandridge]] and [[Wheathampstead]], transferred from the abolished constituency of [[Hitchin and Harpenden (UK Parliament constituency)|Hitchin and Harpenden]] * [[Berkhamsted]] and [[Tring]], transferred from [[South West Hertfordshire (UK Parliament constituency)|South West Hertfordshire]] * A sparsely populated rural area connecting the above two areas, transferred from [[Hemel Hempstead (UK Parliament constituency)|Hemel Hempstead]]<ref>{{Cite web |title=New Seat Details - Harpenden and Berkhamsted |url=https://www.electoralcalculus.co.uk/fcgi-bin/calcwork23.py?seat=Harpenden+and+Berkhamsted |access-date=2024-02-10 |website=www.electoralcalculus.co.uk}}</ref> Following a local government boundary review which came into effect in May 2022,<ref>{{Cite web |last=LGBCE |title=St Albans {{!}} LGBCE |url=https://www.lgbce.org.uk/all-reviews/st-albans |access-date=2024-04-07 |website=www.lgbce.org.uk |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=The St Albans (Electoral Changes) Order 2021 |url=https://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/2021/900/contents/made}}</ref> the parts in the City of St Albans now comprise the following wards from the 2024 general election:
* Harpenden East; Harpenden North & Rural; Harpenden South; Harpenden West; Marshalswick East & Jersey Farm (part); Redbourn; Sandridge & Wheathampstead; and very small parts of the Marshalswick West, St Stephen and Verulam wards.<ref>{{Cite web |title=New Seat Details - Harpenden and Berkhamsted |url=https://www.electoralcalculus.co.uk/fcgi-bin/calcwork23.py?seat=Harpenden+and+Berkhamsted |access-date=2024-04-07 |website=www.electoralcalculus.co.uk}}</ref>
